---
id: no-async-client-component
title: Disallow async components in client context
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Async React components are only valid within React Server Components."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In TanStack Start, that means async components must only be used in server-component context, for example:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"rendered by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderServerComponent(<AsyncComp />)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"rendered inside a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createCompositeComponent((props) => <AsyncComp />)"},{"type":"text","value":" callback"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This rule helps you catch async components that have become \"client\" (directly or transitively), which would otherwise crash at runtime."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"rule-details","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rule Details"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples of "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"incorrect"}]},{"type":"text","value":" code for this rule:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"/* eslint \"@tanstack/start/no-async-client-component\": \"error\" */\n\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport async function Page() {\n  return <div />\n}\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute(undefined)({\n  component: Page,\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples of "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"correct"}]},{"type":"text","value":" code for this rule:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"/* eslint \"@tanstack/start/no-async-client-component\": \"error\" */\n\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport function Page() {\n  return <div />\n}\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute(undefined)({\n  component: Page,\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"code","value":"/* eslint \"@tanstack/start/no-async-client-component\": \"error\" */\n\nimport { createCompositeComponent } from '@tanstack/react-start/rsc'\n\nexport const ServerPage = createCompositeComponent(async () => {\n  const message = await Promise.resolve('hello')\n  return <div>{message}</div>\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"reporting-location","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reporting location"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This rule can report in two ways:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Usage-site"}]},{"type":"text","value":": if a component becomes client due to being referenced by route options, the error should be reported at the route option usage."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Definition-site"}]},{"type":"text","value":": if a component is client due to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'use client'"},{"type":"text","value":" or being rendered by a client component, the error is reported at the component definition."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"attributes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Attributes"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"✅ Recommended"}]}],"checked":true}]}],"headings":[{"id":"rule-details","text":"Rule Details","level":2},{"id":"reporting-location","text":"Reporting location","level":2},{"id":"attributes","text":"Attributes","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nAsync React components are only valid within React Server Components.\n\nIn TanStack Start, that means async components must only be used in server-component context, for example:\n\n- rendered by `renderServerComponent(<AsyncComp />)`\n- rendered inside a `createCompositeComponent((props) => <AsyncComp />)` callback\n\nThis rule helps you catch async components that have become \"client\" (directly or transitively), which would otherwise crash at runtime.\n\n## Rule Details\n\nExamples of **incorrect** code for this rule:\n\n```tsx\n/* eslint \"@tanstack/start/no-async-client-component\": \"error\" */\n\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport async function Page() {\n  return <div />\n}\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute(undefined)({\n  component: Page,\n})\n```\n\nExamples of **correct** code for this rule:\n\n```tsx\n/* eslint \"@tanstack/start/no-async-client-component\": \"error\" */\n\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport function Page() {\n  return <div />\n}\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute(undefined)({\n  component: Page,\n})\n```\n\n```tsx\n/* eslint \"@tanstack/start/no-async-client-component\": \"error\" */\n\nimport { createCompositeComponent } from '@tanstack/react-start/rsc'\n\nexport const ServerPage = createCompositeComponent(async () => {\n  const message = await Promise.resolve('hello')\n  return <div>{message}</div>\n})\n```\n\n## Reporting location\n\nThis rule can report in two ways:\n\n- **Usage-site**: if a component becomes client due to being referenced by route options, the error should be reported at the route option usage.\n- **Definition-site**: if a component is client due to `'use client'` or being rendered by a client component, the error is reported at the component definition.\n\n## Attributes\n\n- [x] ✅ Recommended\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: no-async-client-component\ntitle: Disallow async components in client context\n---\n\nAsync React components are only valid within React Server Components.\n\nIn TanStack Start, that means async components must only be used in server-component context, for example:\n\n- rendered by `renderServerComponent(<AsyncComp />)`\n- rendered inside a `createCompositeComponent((props) => <AsyncComp />)` callback\n\nThis rule helps you catch async components that have become \"client\" (directly or transitively), which would otherwise crash at runtime.\n\n## Rule Details\n\nExamples of **incorrect** code for this rule:\n\n```tsx\n/* eslint \"@tanstack/start/no-async-client-component\": \"error\" */\n\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport async function Page() {\n  return <div />\n}\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute(undefined)({\n  component: Page,\n})\n```\n\nExamples of **correct** code for this rule:\n\n```tsx\n/* eslint \"@tanstack/start/no-async-client-component\": \"error\" */\n\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport function Page() {\n  return <div />\n}\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute(undefined)({\n  component: Page,\n})\n```\n\n```tsx\n/* eslint \"@tanstack/start/no-async-client-component\": \"error\" */\n\nimport { createCompositeComponent } from '@tanstack/react-start/rsc'\n\nexport const ServerPage = createCompositeComponent(async () => {\n  const message = await Promise.resolve('hello')\n  return <div>{message}</div>\n})\n```\n\n## Reporting location\n\nThis rule can report in two ways:\n\n- **Usage-site**: if a component becomes client due to being referenced by route options, the error should be reported at the route option usage.\n- **Definition-site**: if a component is client due to `'use client'` or being rendered by a client component, the error is reported at the component definition.\n\n## Attributes\n\n- [x] ✅ Recommended\n"}
